IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ndis-comp-dates`

-- National Disability Insurance Scheme Act 2013 (Cth) -- compensation for a personal injury and the NDIS: what counts as
-- compensation (s 11); the CEO's power to require a participant or prospective participant to take action to claim
-- compensation, the duty to take it, and what follows if it is not taken (ss 104, 105); a claim taken over by the CEO,
-- its costs and the balance paid to the person (ss 105A(1), 105B); the recoverable amount repaid out of a judgement,
-- consent judgement or settlement, and the debt it creates (ss 106, 107, 108); notices to the person claimed against and
-- its insurer, what they may pay the person, how much the Agency may recover from them, and the discharge that follows
-- (ss 109-114); the CEO's power to disregard part of a payment (s 116); review of these decisions (s 99, items 23-28;
-- s 100(2)); and, for the debt, the time limit on recovery proceedings and the waivers (ss 183, 193, 194, 195).
--
-- SEAT: the person with disability who has, or may have, a claim for compensation for a personal injury -- a
-- participant, or a prospective participant (one whose access request has been made but not yet decided). Every
-- question is phrased as that person asks it ("Can the CEO make me ...?", "How much must I repay?"). Where the Act
-- addresses the CEO, the Agency, the person claimed against (the "compensation payer") or its insurer, it is encoded as
-- what that means for the person: what can be required of them, what they keep, what they owe and by when.
-- Where the Act hands a judgement to the CEO (the opinion that the person may be entitled to compensation, reasonable
-- prospects of success, that an agreement giving up the right is void, special circumstances), it is asked as an input:
-- "if the CEO is satisfied that ...".
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 26, compilation date 27 August 2026 (includes amendments up to Act No. 66, 2026), register id
-- C2026C00366, deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2013A00020.txt. The deposit's caveat: a version in force from
-- 19 September 2026 had no registered compilation when it was retrieved, so later amendments may be missing.
-- The NDIS rules are not deposited. Anything they prescribe (other laws whose charges come off the compensation under
-- ss 106(5)(b)(iv), 107(4)(b)(iv); a period for review under s 100(6A)) is an input or out.
--
-- The earlier encoding beside this one (../baseline-2026-10, access to the scheme) is untouched; this folder adds a layer.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `National Disability Insurance Scheme Act 2013 -- compensation`

§§ `s 11 -- what counts as compensation`

-- s 11(1): "compensation means a payment (with or without admission of liability) in respect of: (a) compensation or
-- damages in respect of personal injury; or (b) personal injury, under a scheme of insurance or compensation under a
-- Commonwealth, State or Territory law ...; or (c) personal injury, in settlement of a claim for damages or a claim
-- under such an insurance scheme; that is wholly or partly in respect of the cost of supports that may be provided to a
-- participant (whether or not specifically identified as such)." s 11(2): a lump sum or periodic payments, made within
-- or outside Australia. Gloss: an admission of liability, the form of payment, the place and the payee do not matter.
DECLARE `What the payment is for` IS ONE OF
    `compensation or damages for a personal injury`
    `a personal injury, under a Commonwealth, State or Territory insurance or compensation scheme`
    `a personal injury, in settlement of a claim for damages or under such a scheme`
    `something else`

-- A "means" definition: where it is not met the answer is no.
@export Is this payment "compensation" under the NDIS Act (s 11)?
GIVEN `what the payment is for` IS A `What the payment is for` @desc What the payment is for. One of: "compensation or damages for a personal injury", "a personal injury, under a Commonwealth, State or Territory insurance or compensation scheme", "a personal injury, in settlement of a claim for damages or under such a scheme", "something else"
      `it is wholly or partly for the cost of supports` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment wholly or partly for the cost of supports that could be provided to you, whether or not it says so?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this payment compensation` IF
        (NOT (`what the payment is for` EQUALS `something else`))
    AND `it is wholly or partly for the cost of supports`

§§ `s 104 -- the CEO may require me to take action to claim compensation`

-- "participant": a person who is a participant in the scheme (s 9). "prospective participant": a person in relation to
-- whom an access request has been made but not yet decided (s 9).
DECLARE `My standing in the scheme` IS ONE OF
    `a participant`
    `a prospective participant`
    `neither`

-- s 104(1)(b): "(i) has taken no action to claim or obtain the compensation; or (ii) has taken no reasonable action".
DECLARE `What I have done to claim` IS ONE OF
    `nothing`
    `nothing reasonable`
    `reasonable action`

-- s 104(1): the section "applies if" the person is a participant or prospective participant who is, or in the CEO's
-- opinion may be, entitled to compensation for a personal injury, and has taken no (reasonable) action to claim it.
-- s 104(4): "The CEO must not give a notice ... unless the CEO is satisfied that the participant or prospective
-- participant has reasonable prospects of success". s 104(6): "Even though [the person] has entered into an agreement to
-- give up his or her right to compensation, the CEO may form the opinion that [the person] may be entitled to
-- compensation if the CEO is satisfied that the agreement is void, ineffective or unenforceable."
-- The answer is whether the CEO MAY give the notice; whether the action required is reasonable (s 104(2), (3)) is the
-- CEO's judgement on the matters in s 104(3), not decided here.
-- FORK: an agreement giving up the right that the CEO is not satisfied is void. s 104(6) says when the CEO "may" form the
-- opinion despite the agreement, not that it may not otherwise: NOTHING (the text does not say). Other reading: the
-- agreement stops the opinion, so the answer is no.
@export Can the CEO require me, by written notice, to take action to claim compensation for my injury (s 104)?
GIVEN `my standing` IS A `My standing in the scheme` @desc Are you in the NDIS? One of: "a participant", "a prospective participant" (your access request is made but not yet decided), "neither"
      `the CEO considers I am or may be entitled to compensation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, or in the CEO's opinion may you be, entitled to compensation for a personal injury?
      `what I have done` IS A `What I have done to claim` @desc What have you done to claim or obtain that compensation? One of: "nothing", "nothing reasonable", "reasonable action"
      `I have agreed to give up my right to compensation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you entered into an agreement giving up your right to that compensation?
      `the CEO is satisfied the agreement is void` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, is the CEO satisfied the agreement is void, ineffective or unenforceable? (Answer no if there is no agreement.)
      `the CEO is satisfied I have reasonable prospects` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the CEO satisfied you have reasonable prospects of success in claiming or obtaining the compensation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the CEO require me to take action to claim compensation` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `my standing` EQUALS `neither` THEN JUST FALSE
        IF (NOT `the CEO considers I am or may be entitled to compensation`) THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `I have agreed to give up my right to compensation` AND (NOT `the CEO is satisfied the agreement is void`) THEN NOTHING
        IF `what I have done` EQUALS `reasonable action` THEN JUST FALSE
        IF (NOT `the CEO is satisfied I have reasonable prospects`) THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `ss 104(5), (5A), 105(1) -- the duty to take the required action, and by when`

-- s 104(5): "The period specified by the CEO must be a period of at least 28 days after the day on which the notice is
-- given." s 104(5A): the CEO may, on the person's application, extend it. s 105(1): the person "must take the required
-- action within the period". Gloss: a period of N days after the day the notice is given ends on the Nth day after it.
-- FORK: a notice giving fewer than 28 days. s 104(5) binds the CEO and says nothing of the person's deadline then:
-- NOTHING. Other reading: the period is read up to 28 days.
`the shortest period a notice may give` MEANS 28

GIVEN `the notice period` IS A NUMBER, `the extension` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the days I have` MEANS
    IF `the notice period` LESS THAN `the shortest period a notice may give`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the notice period` PLUS `the extension`)

@export By when must I take the action a s 104 notice requires (ss 104(5), (5A), 105(1))?
GIVEN `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE @desc The day the CEO's s 104 notice was given to you (ISO date, e.g. 2026-11-02)
      `the notice period` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days after that day the notice gives you to act
      `the extension` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days the CEO has extended the period by on your application (0 if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `By when must I take the required action` IS
    CONSIDER `the days I have` `the notice period` `the extension`
    WHEN JUST n THEN JUST (`the day N days after` `the day the notice was given` n)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- The parties and the one action of the s 105(1) duty.
DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the participant or prospective participant`
    `the CEO`

DECLARE `Compensation action` IS ONE OF
    `take the required action`

-- s 105(1) as a regulative rule, counted in days from the day the notice is given.
GIVEN `the days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Compensation action`
`the s 105(1) duty` MEANS
    PARTY `the participant or prospective participant`
    MUST `take the required action`
    WITHIN `the days`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the participant or prospective participant` BECAUSE "the required action was not taken within the period the notice specified (s 105(1))"

GIVEN `the days` IS A NUMBER, `I took it` IS A BOOLEAN, `days after the notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the duty is fulfilled` MEANS
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`the s 105(1) duty` `the days`) 0 `the events`
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHERE
        `the events` MEANS
            IF `I took it`
            THEN LIST EVENT `the participant or prospective participant` `take the required action` `days after the notice`
            ELSE LIST WAITUNTIL (`the days` PLUS 1)

@export Have I complied with a s 104 notice by taking the required action in time (s 105(1))?
GIVEN `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE @desc The day the CEO's s 104 notice was given to you (ISO date)
      `the notice period` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days after that day the notice gives you to act
      `the extension` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days the CEO has extended the period by (0 if none)
      `I have taken the required action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you taken the action the notice requires?
      `the day I took it` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day you took it (ISO date; any date if you have not)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I taken the required action in time` IS
    CONSIDER `the days I have` `the notice period` `the extension`
    WHEN JUST n THEN JUST (`the duty is fulfilled` n `I have taken the required action` (`days from` `the day the notice was given` `the day I took it`))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

§§ `s 105(2)-(4) -- what follows if I do not take the required action in time`

DECLARE `My standing at the end of the period` IS ONE OF
    `I am a participant`
    `I am a prospective participant`

DECLARE `What happens to my plan` IS ONE OF
    `my plan is not affected`
    `my plan is suspended from the end of the period until I take the required action`
    `my plan is prepared but does not come into effect until I take the required action`
    `my access request may still be decided and my plan prepared, but the plan does not come into effect until I take the required action`

-- s 105(2): "If a participant does not take the required action within the period, and the action is to enable [the
-- person] to claim or obtain compensation under a scheme of compensation under a Commonwealth, State or Territory law:
-- (a) if a plan is in effect ... the plan is suspended from the end of the specified period until the participant takes
-- the required action; or (b) if a plan is not yet in effect ... the plan does not come into effect until the
-- participant takes the required action."
-- s 105(3): "If a prospective participant does not take the required action within the period", the CEO may still decide
-- the access request and start preparing the plan, "but the plan does not ... come into effect until the participant
-- takes the required action." s 105(3) is not limited to statutory schemes (see NOTES.md, finding 3).
GIVEN `I took the required action in time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my standing` IS A `My standing at the end of the period`
      `the compensation is under a statutory scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a plan is in effect for me` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What happens to my plan`
`the plan consequence` MEANS
    IF `I took the required action in time`
    THEN `my plan is not affected`
    ELSE CONSIDER `my standing`
         WHEN `I am a prospective participant` THEN `my access request may still be decided and my plan prepared, but the plan does not come into effect until I take the required action`
         WHEN `I am a participant` THEN
             IF `the compensation is under a statutory scheme`
             THEN IF `a plan is in effect for me`
                  THEN `my plan is suspended from the end of the period until I take the required action`
                  ELSE `my plan is prepared but does not come into effect until I take the required action`
             ELSE `my plan is not affected`

@export If I do not take the action a s 104 notice requires in time, what happens to my NDIS plan (s 105(2), (3))?
GIVEN `I took the required action in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you take the required action within the period (as extended)?
      `my standing` IS A `My standing at the end of the period` @desc At the end of the period, were you "I am a participant" or "I am a prospective participant" (access request not yet decided)?
      `the compensation is under a statutory scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the compensation claimed under a scheme of compensation under a Commonwealth, State or Territory law (for example a workers compensation or transport accident scheme), rather than a common law claim?
      `a plan is in effect for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an NDIS plan in effect for you at the end of the period?
GIVETH A `What happens to my plan`
DECIDE `What happens to my plan if I do not act` IS
    `the plan consequence` `I took the required action in time` `my standing` `the compensation is under a statutory scheme` `a plan is in effect for me`

-- s 105(4): if the person does not take the required action within the period, "and the action is to enable the person
-- to claim or obtain compensation otherwise than under a scheme of compensation under a Commonwealth, State or Territory
-- law, the CEO may: (a) take action to claim or obtain compensation in the name of the participant or prospective
-- participant; or (b) take over the conduct of any existing claim."
-- s 105(6): "The CEO must not take any action ..., or take over the conduct of an existing claim, unless: (a) the CEO has
-- notified the participant or prospective participant, in writing, that the action is being considered; and (b) 28 days
-- have passed since the notice was given." The s 105(5) matters the CEO must weigh are the CEO's judgement, not decided.
-- INFERENCE: "28 days have passed since the notice was given" counts whole days after the day of the notice, so the CEO
-- may act on the 29th day after it at the earliest.
`the days that must pass after the CEO's warning` MEANS 28

@export Can the CEO now claim compensation in my name, or take over my existing claim (s 105(4), (6))?
GIVEN `I took the required action in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you take the action the s 104 notice required within the period (as extended)?
      `the compensation is under a statutory scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the compensation claimed under a Commonwealth, State or Territory scheme of compensation (rather than, for example, a common law claim for damages)?
      `the CEO has warned me in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the CEO told you in writing that it is considering claiming in your name or taking over your claim?
      `the day of the warning` IS A DATE @desc The day that written notice was given to you (ISO date; any date if none)
      `the day the CEO would act` IS A DATE @desc The day the CEO would claim or take over your claim (ISO date)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the CEO claim in my name or take over my claim` IF
        (NOT `I took the required action in time`)
    AND (NOT `the compensation is under a statutory scheme`)
    AND `the CEO has warned me in writing`
    AND `days from` `the day of the warning` `the day the CEO would act` GREATER THAN `the days that must pass after the CEO's warning`

§§ `ss 105A(1), 105B -- a claim the CEO makes or takes over`

-- s 105A(1): the Agency "becomes liable to pay all costs of and incidental to that claim that would otherwise be payable
-- by the person who originally made the claim, or the person in whose name the claim was made, other than costs
-- unreasonably incurred by that person." INFERENCE: costs unreasonably incurred stay with the person.
@export How much of the costs of a claim the CEO makes or takes over does the Agency pay (s 105A(1))?
GIVEN `the costs I would otherwise pay` IS A NUMBER @desc The costs of and incidental to the claim that you would otherwise have to pay, in dollars
      `the costs I incurred unreasonably` IS A NUMBER @desc The part of those costs you incurred unreasonably, in dollars (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of the costs does the Agency pay` IS
    max 0 (`the costs I would otherwise pay` MINUS `the costs I incurred unreasonably`)

-- s 105B: any amount obtained on a claim made or taken over by the CEO is paid to the Agency, which "must deduct ...
-- (a) an amount equal to the total of all NDIS amounts paid to, or for the benefit of, the participant before the amount
-- is paid to the Agency; and (b) the amount of any costs incidental to the claim paid by the Agency. The Agency must pay
-- the balance to the participant or prospective participant." "NDIS amount": an amount paid under the scheme for
-- supports (other than general supports) funded under a participant's plan (s 9).
-- INFERENCE: where the deductions exceed the amount obtained, the balance is nil; s 105B does not make the person pay
-- the shortfall.
@export How much of the money obtained on a claim the CEO made or took over is paid to me (s 105B)?
GIVEN `the amount obtained` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount obtained on the claim (including under a settlement), in dollars
      `the NDIS amounts paid for me` IS A NUMBER @desc The total NDIS amounts paid to you or for your benefit before the amount was paid to the Agency, in dollars
      `the costs the Agency paid` IS A NUMBER @desc The costs incidental to the claim that the Agency paid, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of the amount obtained is paid to me` IS
    max 0 ((`the amount obtained` MINUS `the NDIS amounts paid for me`) MINUS `the costs the Agency paid`)

§§ `ss 106, 107, 108, 116 -- repaying past NDIS amounts out of a judgement or settlement`

DECLARE `How the compensation was fixed` IS ONE OF
    `by a judgement that was not by consent`
    `by a consent judgement`
    `by a settlement`
    `it has not been fixed`

-- s 106(1) (a judgement other than a consent judgement) and s 107(1) (a consent judgement or settlement) apply if an
-- amount of compensation is fixed in respect of a personal injury "that has caused, to any extent, a participant's
-- impairment (whether or not the participant was a participant at the time of the injury)", and NDIS amounts (the past
-- NDIS amounts) had been paid for supports for the impairment before the day of the judgement or settlement. s 106(1)(c)
-- adds: "the judgement specifies a portion (the past NDIS support component) of the amount of compensation to be a
-- component for supports of a kind funded or provided under the" scheme.
-- s 116: "the CEO may treat the whole or part of a compensation payment as not having been fixed by a judgement ... or
-- settlement, if the CEO thinks it is appropriate to do so in the special circumstances of the case." Asked as the part
-- the CEO has so treated; INFERENCE: that part comes off the compensation fixed, and if it is the whole, nothing is fixed.
GIVEN `how fixed` IS A `How the compensation was fixed`
      `the injury caused my impairment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the compensation fixed` IS A NUMBER
      `the part disregarded` IS A NUMBER
      `the past NDIS amounts` IS A NUMBER
      `the judgement specifies a past NDIS support component` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a recoverable amount arises` IF
        (NOT (`how fixed` EQUALS `it has not been fixed`))
    AND `the injury caused my impairment`
    AND `the compensation fixed` MINUS `the part disregarded` GREATER THAN 0
    AND `the past NDIS amounts` GREATER THAN 0
    AND (    (NOT (`how fixed` EQUALS `by a judgement that was not by consent`))
          OR `the judgement specifies a past NDIS support component`)

-- s 106(2), 107(2): the recoverable amount is the sum of the past NDIS amounts, reduced under (3), unless (4) or (5)
-- (s 107: (4)) applies.
-- s 106(3), 107(3): if liability was apportioned between the participant and another person and, as a result, the
-- compensation is less, "the sum of the past NDIS amounts is to be reduced by the proportion corresponding to the
-- proportion of liability that is apportioned to the participant".
-- s 106(4): if the amount would exceed the past NDIS support component, it is "the lesser of the sum of the past NDIS
-- amounts and the past NDIS support component" (which is the component, since the past amounts are then larger).
-- s 106(5), 107(4): if the amount would exceed "the difference (if any) between: (a) the amount of compensation fixed ...;
-- and (b) the sum of the amounts (if any) payable in respect of the amount of compensation under" the Health and Other
-- Services (Compensation) Act 1995, the Care Charges Act 1995, Part 3.14 of the Social Security Act 1991 and laws the
-- rules prescribe, it is that difference. INFERENCE: with no difference (the charges use up the compensation) the
-- recoverable amount is nil. Where both s 106(4) and (5) bite, s 106(2)(b)'s "whichever of those subsections is
-- applicable" does not say which; each is a ceiling, so the lesser is taken (NOTES.md, finding 5).
GIVEN `how fixed` IS A `How the compensation was fixed`
      `the injury caused my impairment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the compensation fixed` IS A NUMBER
      `the part disregarded` IS A NUMBER
      `the past NDIS amounts` IS A NUMBER
      `the judgement specifies a past NDIS support component` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the past NDIS support component` IS A NUMBER
      `liability was apportioned to me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my share of liability` IS A NUMBER
      `the other charges on the compensation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the recoverable amount` MEANS
    IF `a recoverable amount arises` `how fixed` `the injury caused my impairment` `the compensation fixed` `the part disregarded` `the past NDIS amounts` `the judgement specifies a past NDIS support component`
    THEN IF `how fixed` EQUALS `by a judgement that was not by consent`
         THEN min (min `the reduced sum` `the past NDIS support component`) `the difference`
         ELSE min `the reduced sum` `the difference`
    ELSE 0
    WHERE
        `the reduced sum` MEANS
            IF `liability was apportioned to me`
            THEN `the past NDIS amounts` TIMES ((100 MINUS `my share of liability`) DIVIDED BY 100)
            ELSE `the past NDIS amounts`
        `the difference` MEANS
            max 0 ((`the compensation fixed` MINUS `the part disregarded`) MINUS `the other charges on the compensation`)

-- s 108: "An amount payable by a person under section 106 or 107 is a debt due by the person to the Agency."
@export Does my compensation judgement or settlement make me liable to repay past NDIS amounts to the Agency (ss 106, 107, 108)? The amount may still be nil; ask "How much must I repay".
GIVEN `how fixed` IS A `How the compensation was fixed` @desc How was your compensation fixed? One of: "by a judgement that was not by consent", "by a consent judgement", "by a settlement", "it has not been fixed"
      `the injury caused my impairment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the personal injury cause, to any extent, the impairment for which you are an NDIS participant (whether or not you were a participant at the time of the injury)?
      `the compensation fixed` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of compensation fixed by the judgement or settlement, in dollars
      `the part disregarded` IS A NUMBER @desc The part of it the CEO has decided to treat as not fixed by a judgement or settlement under s 116, in dollars (0 if none)
      `the past NDIS amounts` IS A NUMBER @desc The NDIS amounts paid for supports for your impairment before the day of the judgement or settlement, in dollars
      `the judgement specifies a past NDIS support component` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a judgement not by consent: does it specify a part of the compensation as being for supports of a kind the NDIS funds or provides? (Answer no otherwise.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I owe the Agency a recoverable amount` IS
    `a recoverable amount arises` `how fixed` `the injury caused my impairment` `the compensation fixed` `the part disregarded` `the past NDIS amounts` `the judgement specifies a past NDIS support component`

@export How much must I repay the Agency out of my compensation judgement or settlement (ss 106, 107, 108)?
GIVEN `how fixed` IS A `How the compensation was fixed` @desc How was your compensation fixed? One of: "by a judgement that was not by consent", "by a consent judgement", "by a settlement", "it has not been fixed"
      `the injury caused my impairment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the personal injury cause, to any extent, the impairment for which you are an NDIS participant?
      `the compensation fixed` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of compensation fixed by the judgement or settlement, in dollars
      `the part disregarded` IS A NUMBER @desc The part of it the CEO has decided to treat as not fixed under s 116, in dollars (0 if none)
      `the past NDIS amounts` IS A NUMBER @desc The NDIS amounts paid for supports for your impairment before the day of the judgement or settlement, in dollars
      `the judgement specifies a past NDIS support component` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a judgement not by consent: does it specify a part of the compensation as being for supports of a kind the NDIS funds or provides? (Answer no otherwise.)
      `the past NDIS support component` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, that part, in dollars (0 otherwise)
      `liability was apportioned to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was liability for the injury apportioned between you and someone else, so that your compensation is less than it would otherwise have been (contributory negligence)?
      `my share of liability` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, the percentage of liability apportioned to you, e.g. 25 (0 otherwise)
      `the other charges on the compensation` IS A NUMBER @desc The total payable out of the compensation under the Health and Other Services (Compensation) Act 1995, the Health and Other Services (Compensation) Care Charges Act 1995, Part 3.14 of the Social Security Act 1991 and any law the NDIS rules prescribe, in dollars (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much must I repay the Agency` IS
    `the recoverable amount` `how fixed` `the injury caused my impairment` `the compensation fixed` `the part disregarded` `the past NDIS amounts` `the judgement specifies a past NDIS support component` `the past NDIS support component` `liability was apportioned to me` `my share of liability` `the other charges on the compensation`

§§ `ss 109-114 -- notices to the person I claim against, and what they may pay me`

-- s 110(1), (3): the person claimed against (the potential compensation payer), given a s 109(1) preliminary notice,
-- must give the CEO written notice of its liability to pay the person compensation "within 7 days after becoming liable
-- or receiving the notice, whichever is later" (an offence: 12 months or 60 penalty units, or both; or a civil penalty
-- of 60 penalty units). s 110(2), (4) put the same duty on its insurer. Encoded for the person: by when the Agency must
-- be told that the person they claim against is liable to them.
@export By when must the person I claim against tell the NDIA CEO that it has become liable to pay me compensation (s 110)?
GIVEN `the day it received the preliminary notice` IS A DATE @desc The day the person you claim against (or its insurer) received the CEO's s 109 preliminary notice (ISO date)
      `the day it became liable` IS A DATE @desc The day it became liable to pay you compensation (or the insurer became liable to indemnify it) (ISO date)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must the person I claim against tell the CEO` IS
    `the day N days after` `the later day` 7
    WHERE
        `the later day` MEANS
            IF `days from` `the day it received the preliminary notice` `the day it became liable` GREATER THAN 0
            THEN `the day it became liable`
            ELSE `the day it received the preliminary notice`

DECLARE `The CEO's notice to the person I claim against` IS ONE OF
    `no notice`
    `a preliminary notice under s 109`
    `a recovery notice under s 111`

DECLARE `Can I be paid` IS ONE OF
    `the NDIS Act does not stop the payment`
    `it must not pay me while the notice has effect`

-- s 112: a person (or insurer) given a s 109 or s 111 notice "is not liable to pay that compensation while the notice has
-- effect". s 114(1), (3), (5), (7): making the payment to the participant or prospective participant is an offence and a
-- civil penalty contravention, unless (s 114(2), (4), (6), (8)): "(a) in the case of a notice under section 109 -- the CEO
-- has given [it] written notice that the notice is revoked; or (b) in the case of a notice under section 111 -- [it] has
-- paid to the Agency the amount specified in the notice; or (c) the CEO has given [it] written permission to pay the
-- amount." A flat negative ("commits an offence if ... makes the compensation payment"), so the answer is that it must not.
@export Can the person I claim against (or its insurer) pay me my compensation now, after the CEO has sent it a notice (ss 112, 114)?
GIVEN `the notice` IS A `The CEO's notice to the person I claim against` @desc Which notice has the CEO given the person you claim against (or its insurer)? One of: "no notice", "a preliminary notice under s 109", "a recovery notice under s 111"
      `the CEO has revoked the preliminary notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a s 109 notice: has the CEO given it written notice that the notice is revoked?
      `it has paid the Agency the amount in the recovery notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a s 111 notice: has it paid the Agency the amount specified in the notice?
      `the CEO has permitted it to pay me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the CEO given it written permission to pay you the amount?
GIVETH A `Can I be paid`
DECIDE `Can the person I claim against pay me now` IS
    CONSIDER `the notice`
    WHEN `no notice` THEN `the NDIS Act does not stop the payment`
    WHEN `a preliminary notice under s 109` THEN
        IF `the CEO has revoked the preliminary notice` OR `the CEO has permitted it to pay me`
        THEN `the NDIS Act does not stop the payment`
        ELSE `it must not pay me while the notice has effect`
    WHEN `a recovery notice under s 111` THEN
        IF `it has paid the Agency the amount in the recovery notice` OR `the CEO has permitted it to pay me`
        THEN `the NDIS Act does not stop the payment`
        ELSE `it must not pay me while the notice has effect`

-- s 111(4): "The amount to be specified in the notice is the lesser of the following: (a) an amount equal to the sum of
-- the NDIS amounts referred to in paragraph (1)(a) or (2)(a) [paid in respect of the participant's impairment]; (b) an
-- amount equal to the recoverable amount in relation to the judgement, consent judgement or settlement to which the
-- liability relates." s 111(6): it applies even if the compensation is inalienable.
-- FORK: where there is no judgement or settlement yet, or s 106 does not apply to the judgement (no past NDIS support
-- component), there is no "recoverable amount in relation to the judgement", and the text does not say what the notice
-- may then specify: NOTHING. Other reading: limb (b) drops out and the sum of the NDIS amounts is the amount.
@export How much can the Agency recover from the person I claim against (or its insurer) by a recovery notice (s 111(4))?
GIVEN `the NDIS amounts paid for my impairment` IS A NUMBER @desc The total NDIS amounts paid in respect of your impairment, in dollars
      `how fixed` IS A `How the compensation was fixed` @desc How was your compensation fixed? One of: "by a judgement that was not by consent", "by a consent judgement", "by a settlement", "it has not been fixed"
      `the injury caused my impairment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the personal injury cause, to any extent, your impairment?
      `the compensation fixed` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of compensation fixed, in dollars (0 if not fixed)
      `the part disregarded` IS A NUMBER @desc The part the CEO has decided to treat as not fixed under s 116, in dollars (0 if none)
      `the past NDIS amounts` IS A NUMBER @desc The NDIS amounts paid for supports for your impairment before the day of the judgement or settlement, in dollars
      `the judgement specifies a past NDIS support component` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a judgement not by consent: does it specify a part of the compensation as being for NDIS-type supports? (Answer no otherwise.)
      `the past NDIS support component` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, that part, in dollars (0 otherwise)
      `liability was apportioned to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was liability apportioned to you, reducing your compensation?
      `my share of liability` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, your percentage of liability, e.g. 25 (0 otherwise)
      `the other charges on the compensation` IS A NUMBER @desc The total payable out of the compensation under the Health and Other Services (Compensation) Acts, Part 3.14 of the Social Security Act 1991 and laws the rules prescribe, in dollars (0 if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much can the Agency recover from the person I claim against` IS
    IF `a recoverable amount arises` `how fixed` `the injury caused my impairment` `the compensation fixed` `the part disregarded` `the past NDIS amounts` `the judgement specifies a past NDIS support component`
    THEN JUST (min `the NDIS amounts paid for my impairment` (`the recoverable amount` `how fixed` `the injury caused my impairment` `the compensation fixed` `the part disregarded` `the past NDIS amounts` `the judgement specifies a past NDIS support component` `the past NDIS support component` `liability was apportioned to me` `my share of liability` `the other charges on the compensation`))
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 113(1): payment to the Agency of an amount the compensation payer is liable to pay under s 111 "operates, to the
-- extent of the payment, as a discharge of: (a) the compensation payer's liability to pay compensation to the
-- participant; and (b) the participant's liability to pay the Agency." s 113(2) does the same for an insurer's payment.
-- INFERENCE: neither liability goes below nil.
@export After the person I claim against pays the Agency under a recovery notice, how much compensation does it still owe me (s 113)?
GIVEN `the compensation it owed me` IS A NUMBER @desc The compensation the person you claim against was liable to pay you, in dollars
      `the amount it paid the Agency` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount it (or its insurer) paid the Agency under the s 111 recovery notice, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much compensation is still owed to me` IS
    max 0 (`the compensation it owed me` MINUS `the amount it paid the Agency`)

@export After the person I claim against pays the Agency under a recovery notice, how much do I still owe the Agency (s 113)?
GIVEN `what I owed the Agency` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount you were liable to pay the Agency (your recoverable amount), in dollars
      `the amount it paid the Agency` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount the person you claim against (or its insurer) paid the Agency under the s 111 recovery notice, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much do I still owe the Agency` IS
    max 0 (`what I owed the Agency` MINUS `the amount it paid the Agency`)

§§ `ss 99, 100(2) -- review of a compensation decision`

DECLARE `The compensation decision` IS ONE OF
    `a notice requiring me to take action to claim compensation (s 104)`
    `a refusal to extend the period to take that action (s 104(5A))`
    `a decision to claim compensation in my name (s 105(4)(a))`
    `a decision to take over my claim (s 105(4)(b))`
    `a recovery notice to the person I claim against (s 111)`
    `a decision not to disregard part of my compensation (s 116)`
    `the recoverable amount under s 106 or s 107`

-- s 99(1) and its table, items 23-28: the reviewable decisions in Chapter 5 are those six; the decision-maker is the CEO.
-- "reviewable decision has the meaning given by subsections 99(1) and (2)" (s 9): a closed definition, so a recoverable
-- amount, which arises under the Act without a decision, is not one.
@export Can I ask the CEO to review this compensation decision (s 99, items 23-28)?
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `The compensation decision` @desc Which decision? One of: "a notice requiring me to take action to claim compensation (s 104)", "a refusal to extend the period to take that action (s 104(5A))", "a decision to claim compensation in my name (s 105(4)(a))", "a decision to take over my claim (s 105(4)(b))", "a recovery notice to the person I claim against (s 111)", "a decision not to disregard part of my compensation (s 116)", "the recoverable amount under s 106 or s 107"
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I ask for review of this decision` IF
    (NOT (`the decision` EQUALS `the recoverable amount under s 106 or s 107`))

-- s 100(2): "If the person is given a notice under subsection (1) the person must make the request within 3 months after
-- receiving the notice." INFERENCE: the period ends on the same day of the month three months later, or the last day of
-- that month if it has no such day (as in the access encoding beside this one).
@export By when must I ask for review of a compensation decision (s 100(2))?
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `The compensation decision` @desc Which decision? (The same choices as for "Can I ask for review".)
      `the day I received the notice of the decision` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the CEO's written notice of the decision (ISO date)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `By when must I ask for review` IS
    IF `Can I ask for review of this decision` `the decision`
    THEN JUST (`the day N months after` `the day I received the notice of the decision` 3)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `ss 183, 193, 194, 195 -- the debt: time limit and waiver`

-- s 183(2): proceedings to recover a debt "are not to be commenced after the end of the period (the recovery period) of
-- 6 years starting on the first day an Agency officer becomes aware, or could reasonably be expected to have become
-- aware, of the circumstances that gave rise to the debt." (3): if, within the recovery period, part of the debt is
-- paid, proceedings for the balance may be commenced "within the period of 6 years starting on the day of payment".
-- (4): the same from an acknowledgement. (5): if a review of a recovery file or other internal Agency recovery activity
-- occurs within the recovery period, proceedings "may be commenced within the period of 6 years after the end of the
-- activity".
-- Gloss: a 6-year period starting on a day ends six years after the day before it (the day before the sixth
-- anniversary; 28 February for a period starting on 29 February or 1 March); a period "after the end of" a day
-- ends on the sixth anniversary (INFERENCE). Only a payment, acknowledgement or activity within the original recovery
-- period counts: "recovery period" is defined once (NOTES.md, finding 9). The activity is tested by the day it ended
-- (INFERENCE).
`six years in months` MEANS 72

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of 6 years starting on` MEANS
    `the day N months after` (`the day N days after` `the day` (0 MINUS 1)) `six years in months`

@export By when must the Agency start legal proceedings to recover my debt (s 183)?
GIVEN `the day the Agency knew` IS A DATE @desc The first day an Agency officer became aware, or could reasonably be expected to have become aware, of the circumstances that gave rise to the debt (ISO date)
      `I paid part of the debt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you paid part of the debt within 6 years of that day?
      `the day of my last part payment` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day of the last such payment within those 6 years (ISO date; any date if none)
      `I acknowledged the debt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you acknowledged that you owe the debt within 6 years of that day?
      `the day of my last acknowledgement` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day of the last such acknowledgement within those 6 years (ISO date; any date if none)
      `the Agency worked on recovering it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Agency reviewed a file on, or otherwise worked internally on, recovering the debt within those 6 years?
      `the day that work ended` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day the last such activity ended (ISO date; any date if none)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must the Agency sue me for the debt` IS
    `the latest of` `the recovery period's last day` (LIST `from payment`, `from acknowledgement`, `from activity`)
    WHERE
        `the recovery period's last day` MEANS `the last day of 6 years starting on` `the day the Agency knew`
        `from payment` MEANS
            IF `I paid part of the debt` AND `is within the recovery period from` `the day the Agency knew` `the day of my last part payment`
            THEN `the last day of 6 years starting on` `the day of my last part payment`
            ELSE `the recovery period's last day`
        `from acknowledgement` MEANS
            IF `I acknowledged the debt` AND `is within the recovery period from` `the day the Agency knew` `the day of my last acknowledgement`
            THEN `the last day of 6 years starting on` `the day of my last acknowledgement`
            ELSE `the recovery period's last day`
        `from activity` MEANS
            IF `the Agency worked on recovering it` AND `is within the recovery period from` `the day the Agency knew` `the day that work ended`
            THEN `the day N months after` `the day that work ended` `six years in months`
            ELSE `the recovery period's last day`

GIVEN `the day the Agency knew` IS A DATE, `d` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is within the recovery period from` IF
        `days from` `the day the Agency knew` `d` AT LEAST 0
    AND `days from` `d` (`the last day of 6 years starting on` `the day the Agency knew`) AT LEAST 0

GIVEN `first` IS A DATE, `others` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the latest of` MEANS
    CONSIDER `others`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN `first`
    WHEN d FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF `days from` `first` d GREATER THAN 0
        THEN `the latest of` d rest
        ELSE `the latest of` `first` rest

-- s 193: "The CEO may waive the right to recover a debt if: (a) the debt is, or is likely to be, less than $200; and (b)
-- it is not cost effective for the Agency to take action to recover the debt." An "if": otherwise, no.
`the small debt limit` MEANS 200

@export Can the CEO waive my debt to the Agency as a small debt (s 193)?
GIVEN `my debt` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of the debt, or the amount it is likely to be, in dollars
      `recovery is not cost effective` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it not cost effective for the Agency to take action to recover it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my debt be waived as a small debt` IF
        `my debt` LESS THAN `the small debt limit`
    AND `recovery is not cost effective`

DECLARE `How my debt was settled` IS ONE OF
    `the Agency settled a civil action against me for less than the debt`
    `the CEO settled Tribunal proceedings on my paying less than the debt`
    `the Agency recovered at least part and agreed that is in full satisfaction`
    `the CEO agreed that a lesser amount fully satisfies the outstanding debt`
    `none of these`

-- s 194(1), (2): on a settlement of a civil action, or of Administrative Review Tribunal proceedings, for less than the
-- full debt, the CEO "must waive the right to recover the difference between the debt and the amount that is the subject
-- of the settlement". (3): if "(a) the Agency has recovered at least 80% of the original value of a debt ...; and (b) the
-- Agency and the debtor agree that the recovery is in full satisfaction ...; and (c) the debtor cannot repay a greater
-- proportion of the debt; the CEO must waive the remaining 20% or less". (4): on an agreement that an agreed amount
-- fully satisfies the outstanding (unpaid) amount, the CEO must waive the difference (the s 194(5) present-value
-- condition binds the CEO before agreeing, so an agreement made is taken as given).
`the share that must have been recovered` MEANS 80%

@export How much of my debt to the Agency must the CEO waive after a settlement or agreed part recovery (s 194)?
GIVEN `how settled` IS A `How my debt was settled` @desc What happened? One of: "the Agency settled a civil action against me for less than the debt", "the CEO settled Tribunal proceedings on my paying less than the debt", "the Agency recovered at least part and agreed that is in full satisfaction", "the CEO agreed that a lesser amount fully satisfies the outstanding debt", "none of these"
      `the debt` IS A NUMBER @desc The debt, in dollars: the full debt for a settlement, the original value of the debt for a part recovery, or the amount outstanding when an agreement was made
      `the amount paid or agreed` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount that is the subject of the settlement, the amount recovered, or the agreed amount, in dollars
      `I cannot repay more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a part recovery: are you unable to repay a greater proportion of the debt?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my debt must be waived` IS
    CONSIDER `how settled`
    WHEN `the Agency recovered at least part and agreed that is in full satisfaction` THEN
        IF     `the amount paid or agreed` AT LEAST (`the debt` TIMES `the share that must have been recovered`)
           AND `I cannot repay more`
        THEN max 0 (`the debt` MINUS `the amount paid or agreed`)
        ELSE 0
    WHEN `none of these` THEN 0
    OTHERWISE max 0 (`the debt` MINUS `the amount paid or agreed`)

-- s 195: "The CEO may waive the right to recover a debt if: (a) the debt did not result wholly or partly from the debtor or
-- another person knowingly: (i) making a false or misleading statement or representation; or (ii) failing or omitting to
-- comply with this Act ...; and (b) there are special circumstances (other than financial hardship alone) that the CEO is
-- satisfied make waiver appropriate; and (c) the CEO is satisfied that waiver is more appropriate than writing off the
-- debt."
@export Can the CEO waive my debt to the Agency in special circumstances (s 195)?
GIVEN `someone knowingly misled or failed to comply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the debt result, wholly or partly, from you or anyone else knowingly making a false or misleading statement or representation, or knowingly failing to comply with the NDIS Act, regulations or rules?
      `the CEO is satisfied special circumstances make waiver appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the CEO satisfied that there are special circumstances, other than financial hardship alone, that make waiver appropriate?
      `the CEO is satisfied waiver is better than write-off` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the CEO satisfied that waiver is more appropriate than writing the debt off?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my debt be waived in special circumstances` IF
        (NOT `someone knowingly misled or failed to comply`)
    AND `the CEO is satisfied special circumstances make waiver appropriate`
    AND `the CEO is satisfied waiver is better than write-off`
